OREAAAAASUVORK5CYII=</value></data><data name="chkInformHardwareP2Ports.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Default P2 UDP ports on the radio are:
a) Port 1024 into the radio - discovery and general port, this can not be changed
b) Others into the radio 1025-1029 - these can be changed
c) The radio will also use its own output ports 1024-1041 which direct data to the single PC listen port - these can be changed

If the [inform hardware of ports to use] is unchecked, on a router/modem you would port forward as follows
    WANip:1024-1029 &gt; radioip:1024-1029
    you would connect to a specific radio in this case using Thetis as WANip:1024

    you may want to use different external ports, this would also work
    WAN:51000-51005 &gt; radioip:1024-1029
    you would connect to a specific radio in this case using Thetis as WANip:51000
    
    and the radio would also direct everything form its own ports 1025-1041 to the listen port

If the [inform hardware of ports to use] is checked you could do the following
    WANip:6000 &gt; radioip:1024   (as 1024 can no be changed on the radio)
    WANip:6001-6005 &gt; radioip:6001-6005   (the radio is told of the 6000 base and now offsets its port expectation)
    you would connect to a specific radio in this case using Thetis as WANip:6000
    
    and the radio would also direct everything form its own ports 6001-6018 to the listen port

In all cases, if the client Thetis is behind another modem/router, then the listen port should be port forwarded back directly to the PC ip.</value></data>
